.______()    # get the average weight (pre.weight vs. weight6weeks) for each diet type\n","\n","df_weight_per_diet.plot(kind=______)\n","plt.title('Weight Change per Diet Type')\n","plt.ylabel('Weight')\n","plt.xlabel('Diet Type')\n","plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.legend(_____=______)    # legend in the lower left corner"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["df_weight_per_diet = df.groupby('Diet')[['pre.weight', 'weight6weeks']].mean()\n","\n","df_weight_per_diet.plot(kind='bar')\n","plt.title('Weight Change per Diet Type')\n","plt.ylabel('Weight')\n","plt.xlabel('Diet Type')\n","plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.legend(loc='lower left')"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":489},"id":"1TR_kpEYXLR1","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1684975447047,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":1036,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"900de504-3026-49b9-8f52-688c79c64e77"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["<matplotlib.legend.Legend at 0x7f5bd4162290>"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":4},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["In this code, df_weight_per_diet is created by grouping the DataFrame df by the 'Diet' column and calculating the mean values for the 'pre.weight' and 'weight6weeks' columns. Then, using df_weight_per_diet.plot(kind='bar'), a vertical bar chart showing the average weight data for each diet type is made. The remaining lines in the lower left corner determine the title, axis labels, rotation of x-axis tick labels, and legend location."],"metadata":{"id":"c3szdMl1YFhM"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"GyMhwojL1eq3"},"source":["**Problem 2:** In separate horizontal bar charts for males (gender=1) and females (gender=0), show the average change in weight (pre.weight vs. weight6weeks) per diet type.\n","\n","Hint: ax is a parameter in df.plot -> set ax=ax[0] or ax=ax[1]"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":298},"id":"hDhDxxGG1ykH","outputId":"31db428c-afaa-47a5-bfb3-27d82d0065de"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["Text(0.5, 1.0, 'Weight Change per Diet Type for Males')"]},"execution_count":33,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 432x288 with 2 Axes>"]},"metadata":{"needs_background":"light"},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Solution 1: Horizontal Bar Chart\n","# get the average weight (pre.weight vs. weight6weeks) for each diet type for males and females:\n","df_weight_per_diet_male = df[df.______=='1'].groupby('Diet')[[_______, _________]].______()    # males\n","df_weight_per_diet_female = df[df.______=='0'].groupby('Diet')[[_______, _________]].______()    # females\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.______(2, 1, sharex=True)    # subplots\n","df_weight_per_diet_female._____(kind=_____, ax=_____)    # plot female horizontal barchart\n","ax[0].set_title('Weight Change per Diet Type for Females')\n","\n","df_weight_per_diet_male.______(kind=_____, ax=_____)     # plot male horizontal barchart\n","ax[1].set_title('Weight Change per Diet Type for Males')\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["df_weight_per_diet_male = df[df['gender']=='1'].groupby('Diet')[['pre.weight', 'weight6weeks']].mean()  # males\n","df_weight_per_diet_female = df[df['gender']=='0'].groupby('Diet')[['pre.weight', 'weight6weeks']].mean()  # females\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(2, 1, sharex=True)  # subplots\n","df_weight_per_diet_female.plot(kind='barh', ax=ax[0])  # plot female horizontal bar chart\n","ax[0].set_title('Weight Change per Diet Type for Females')\n","\n","df_weight_per_diet_male.plot(kind='barh', ax=ax[1])  # plot male horizontal bar chart\n","ax[1].set_title('Weight Change per Diet Type for Males')"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":469},"id":"Wcxp4PxyY2Bu","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1684975892125,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":841,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"0e1d8e29-3dee-4211-9892-64ee21faab39"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["Text(0.5, 1.0, 'Weight Change per Diet Type for Males')"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":5},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["In this code, df_weight_per_diet_male is generated by filtering the DataFrame df to include only rows with the 'gender' column equal to '1' (males). Following that, the data is grouped by the 'Diet' column, and the mean values for the 'pre.weight' and 'weight6weeks' columns are computed. Similarly, df_weight_per_diet_female is calculated by filtering the DataFrame df to include only rows with the 'gender' column equal to '0' (females) and then calculating the mean values for the 'pre.weight' and 'weight6weeks' columns. after that, fig, ax = plt.subplots(2, 1, sharex=True) makes a figure with two subplots (one for males and one for females) that share the x-axis. The lines that follow, df_weight_per_diet_female.plot(kind='barh', ax=ax[0]) and df_weight_per_diet_male.plot(kind='barh', ax=ax[1]), plot horizontal bar charts for females and males, respectively. To indicate the corresponding subplot, set the ax parameter to ax[0] and ax[1]. Finally, ax[0].set_title('Weight Change per Diet Type for Females') and ax[1].set_title('Weight Change per Diet Type for Males') are used to set the titles for each subplot."],"metadata":{"id":"bdWivqAFZAeq"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1AsYoElF4l8q"},"source":["**Problem 3:** In a scatter plot, show the correlation between Height and pre.weight"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":312},"id":"PPgWO4dw43AW","outputId":"cf4520ad-934e-4f1a-d455-5c90d3d480e5"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["Text(0.5, 1.0, 'pre.weight vs. Height')"]},"execution_count":25,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 432x288 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{"needs_background":"light"},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# solution 1: scatter plot\n","\n","_____.plot(kind=______, x='Height', y='pre.weight')    # scatter plot on height vs pre.weight\n","plt.title('pre.weight vs. Height')"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["df.plot(kind='scatter', x='Height', y='pre.weight')  # scatter plot on height vs pre.weight\n","plt.title('pre.weight vs. Height')"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":489},"id":"959XsSFibAG_","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1684976451959,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":1150,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"1228d45c-e195-46db-eca9-c00cfe1675d4"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["Text(0.5, 1.0, 'pre.weight vs. Height')"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":6},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The DataFrame containing the data is identified by df in this code. To generate a scatter plot, use the plot function with kind='scatter'. The x-axis is supplied as 'Height' (x='Height'), while the y-axis is specified as 'pre.weight' (y='pre.weight').\n","Finally, plt.title('pre.weight vs. Height') sets the scatter plot's title."],"metadata":{"id":"iuea9x_-bFVy"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"m55aX8s93Yme"},"source":["**Problem 4:** Using a stacked bar chart, show the change in weight for each gender (don't include blank gender). Transfer the legend in the lower left corner\n","\n","Hint: add a weight_change column and plot it with weight6weeks."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":312},"id":"WBkxMEeg3f16","outputId":"e89ad470-f6bb-4dff-a14a-5e5037299235"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["<matplotlib.legend.Legend at 0x7f132ead2e50>"]},"execution_count":38,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 432x288 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{"needs_background":"light"},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["# Solution 1: stacked bar chart\n","\n","# add a weight change column\n","df['weight_change'] = _________ - ___________\n","valid_genders = df[df.______.isin(['1', '0'])]    # don't include blank gender\n","df_weight_per_gender = valid_genders._______('gender')[['weight6weeks', 'weight_change']]._____()    # get average weights per gender\n","\n","df_weight_per_gender.plot(kind='bar', _____=_____)    # stacked bar chart\n","plt.title('Weight Change per Gender')\n","plt.ylabel('Weight')\n","plt.xlabel('Gender')\n","plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.legend(_____=______)    # legend in the lower left corner"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["df['weight_change'] = df['weight6weeks'] - df['pre.weight']\n","valid_genders = df[df['gender'].isin(['1', '0'])]  # don't include blank gender\n","df_weight_per_gender = valid_genders.groupby('gender')[['weight6weeks', 'weight_change']].mean()  # get average weights per gender\n","\n","df_weight_per_gender.plot(kind='bar', stacked=True)  # stacked bar chart\n","plt.title('Weight Change per Gender')\n","plt.ylabel('Weight')\n","plt.xlabel('Gender')\n","plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.legend(loc='lower left')  # legend in the lower left corner"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":489},"id":"lMnpeJgZbqJ-","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1684976622379,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":1257,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"084ad5bf-3fab-4045-f349-aa5698bf30d2"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["<matplotlib.legend.Legend at 0x7f5b96bef970>"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":7},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["By subtracting the 'pre.weight' column from the 'weight6weeks' column, a new column 'weight_change' is created in this code. The DataFrame df is then filtered to include only rows where the 'gender' column is either '1' or '0', eliminating blank genders. After that, the df_weight_per_gender DataFrame is made by grouping the valid_genders DataFrame by the 'gender' column while calculating the mean values for the 'weight6weeks' and 'weight_change' columns. The line df_weight_per_gender.plot(kind='bar, stacked=True) creates a stacked bar chart with the columns 'weight6weeks' and 'weight_change'. To stack the bars, use the stacked=True argument. The remaining lines define the title, axis labels, x-axis tick label rotation, and legend position in the lower left corner."],"metadata":{"id":"elGWcob4buc2"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"D3V--pD-4x8k"},"source":["**Problem 5:** Using a line chart, show the counts of each people with the same age. Sort the index by Age. Add triangle markers and color them red."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":312},"id":"f7iu4Bqh4wdc","outputId":"009ea3b0-8512-4036-8243-179eaa90ca4c"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["Text(0.5, 0, 'Age')"]},"execution_count":50,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 432x288 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{"needs_background":"light"},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["age_count_df = df.Age._______()    # counts of people per age\n","sorted_age_df = age_count_df._______()    # sort the index by age\n","sorted_age_df.plot(marker=____, __________='red', _________='red')    # line chart with red triangle markers\n","plt.title('Count of Volunteers by Age')\n","plt.ylabel('Count')\n","plt.xlabel('Age')"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["age_count_df = df['Age'].value_counts()  # counts of people per age\n","sorted_age_df = age_count_df.sort_index()  # sort the index by age\n","sorted_age_df.plot(marker='^', color='red', markerfacecolor='red')  # line chart with red triangle markers\n","plt.title('Count of Volunteers by Age')\n","plt.ylabel('Count')\n","plt.xlabel('Age')"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":489},"id":"aUzHIypqdDZE","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1684976987767,"user_tz":480,"elapsed":1068,"user":{"displayName":"angeo andaya","userId":"11061685727315027041"}},"outputId":"79c41caa-1390-4a31-c2cb-9b44350a3949"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"execute_result","data":{"text/plain":["Text(0.5, 0, 'Age')"]},"metadata":{},"execution_count":8},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["In this code, age_count_df is created by calculating the counts of persons for each age using the value_counts() function on the 'Age' column. Then, age_count_df is sorted by the index, which reflects the ages, to get sorted_age_df. The line sorted_age_df.plot(marker='', color='red', markerfacecolor='red') function makes a line chart with red triangle markers (given by marker=''). The color='red' argument specifies the color of the line, while the markerfacecolor='red' parameter specifies the color of the marker faces. The remaining lines set the title, axis labels, and the xlabel as 'Age'."],"metadata":{"id":"w1fJz8vhdgIq"}}],"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[{"file_id":"1-5gjmd2uFWCF3yEzJS41BdcYFhw3ZtvK","timestamp":1684975299819},{"file_id":"1Pg_eCUDfgYqGmL_z0_ycHceL729EXBMq","timestamp":1671795846264}]},"kernelspec":